{"case_name": "phrase-dimension-mismatch-fails-whole-concept", "policy_name": "semantic_scoring", "note": "A concept scores the max cosine over its phrases, but one uncomparable phrase fails the whole classifier instead of falling back to the usable ones. 'writes code' matches the input exactly (cosine 1.0, well over the 0.6 threshold) while 'fixes bugs' has a different vector length, so the classifier reports failure, on_error defaults to match_false, and the trace entry carries no score.", "services": {"embed": {"EmbedModel": {"writes code": [1, 0, 0], "fixes bugs": [0, 1], "exactly like writing code": [1, 0, 0]}}}, "request": {"route_trace": true, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "exactly like writing code"}]}, "decision": {"version": "1", "route_to": "DefaultLLM", "matched_rule": "", "default_used": true, "outputs": {}, "trace": [{"condition": "classifier:topic", "label": "coding", "result": false}]}}
